Logical Flow

Snowfall Rules Run - Check for new Violations

Rules run, violations found for rules with “Proactive ServiceNow” ticket enabled

Check DynamoDB table if an active Proactive Case already exists. If so, do nothing.

Create Proactive Case in ServiceNow via SOUP interface. 

Record Proactive Case details (Case Number / Primary Key) in DynamoDB table.

Snowfall Rules Run - Check Previous Violations

Rules run, check if any active Proactive Case in DynamoDB table is no longer in violation. 

Close Proactive Case in ServiceNow via SOUP integration.

Close Proactive Case record in DynamoDB table.

ServiceNow - Proactive Case Closed

Check Case records incoming though existing pipeline for matches with out Proactive Cases in DynamoDB table. 

If Case has been “Resolved”, “Cancelled” or “Closed” in ServiceNow, update DynamoDB table to remove record (or mark as not active). 



Required fields for ServiceNow

The following fields should be included in the payload sent to ServiceNow to create high quality, accurate tickets.

Short Description 

Restaurant Number (from the “restaruant_number” response from the rule)

Description (long form multi-line text field. Ideally the “message” response from the rule)

Service Offering

Category

Subcategory (optional)

Priority (optional, but nice to have)



